@startuml plugin-catalog-architecture
' ============================================================================
'  agentd - Tool Catalog & Plugins (proposed)
'  ONE Tool contract, ONE catalog. Two ORTHOGONAL axes:
'    packaging:  internal (shipped in the app)  vs  plugin (downloaded on demand)
'    impl:       native (a Tool we build)        vs  MCP (an external server/service)
'  -> a 2x2: {internal, plugin} x {native, mcp}. All four normalize to a Tool and
'     land in the SAME catalog; once installed a plugin behaves EXACTLY like an
'     internal tool and is usable by any agent (subject to its allow/deny).
'  Render (from this folder):  java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng plugin-catalog-architecture.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #999999
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  roundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

title agentd - Tool Catalog & Plugins (proposed)\nONE Tool contract, ONE catalog -- packaging (internal vs plugin) and impl (native vs MCP) are ORTHOGONAL\ngreen = exists in v2 today   amber = net-new   gray = port (interface)

' ===========================================================================
' CONSUMER - any agent, filtered view of the one catalog
' ===========================================================================
package "CONSUMER  ·  any agent (domain.select_tools)" #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "ANY AGENT sees the catalog filtered by its OWN tools_allow / tools_deny.\nA plugin tool, once installed, is usable by ANY agent with NO special-casing --\nit flows through the SAME select_tools as every internal tool. [now: filtering exists]" as AGENT #C7B8EA
}

' ===========================================================================
' THE PORT + THE CATALOG - the single normalization point
' ===========================================================================
package "APPLICATION - contract" #E8EAF6 {
  rectangle "PORT: Tool\nname · description · parameters (JSON schema)\nconcurrency · execute(call_id, params, abort, on_update) -> ToolResult\n** EVERY source below normalizes to THIS **" as P_TOOL #E2E2E2
}

package "THE TOOL CATALOG  ·  one merged list" #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "TOOL CATALOG = [Tool]  (all wrapped in GuardedTool: timeout · retry · policy)\nThe loop only ever sees Tool.execute(...). It CANNOT tell internal from plugin,\nnor native from MCP -- they are identical once in the catalog. [now: list+GuardedTool]\n(opt) expose as a `tools.list` surface so clients see all installed tools + who can use them" as CATALOG #BBDEFB
}

' ===========================================================================
' TOOL SOURCES - the 2x2  (internal/plugin  x  native/mcp)
' ===========================================================================
package "TOOL SOURCES  (2x2: packaging x impl)" #E1F5FE {

  package "INTERNAL  -- shipped in the app (lightweight)" #EAF6FF {
    rectangle "internal · NATIVE  [now]\nread · write · exec · browser · web_*\nTool classes in build_tools()" as IN_NATIVE #C8E6C9
    rectangle "internal · MCP  [now, opt]\nMCP server(s) bundled by default\n(declared in config)" as IN_MCP #C8E6C9
  }

  package "PLUGINS  -- downloaded ON DEMAND (heavy / optional)" #FFF3E0 {
    rectangle "plugin · NATIVE  [net-new]\na Python tool we BUILD + package separately\n(e.g. video-edit). Heavy deps in ITS OWN pyproject;\n** imported LAZILY ** only when activated" as PL_NATIVE #FFE0B2
    rectangle "plugin · MCP  [net-new wrapper]\na downloaded MCP-server plugin (e.g. a video MCP /\nany existing service). Deps live in a SEPARATE\nPROCESS -- not in agentd's venv at all" as PL_MCP #FFE0B2
  }
}

' ===========================================================================
' PLUGIN SYSTEM - net-new: manifest + api + discovery/install
' ===========================================================================
package "PLUGIN SYSTEM  (net-new)" #FFF3E0 {
  rectangle "plugin.toml  (manifest)\nid · name · kind = native | mcp\nentry = pkg:register   |   [mcp] command=... / url=...\nconfig_schema · enabled · activation" as MANIFEST #FFE0B2
  rectangle "PORT: PluginApi\nregister_tool(tool)   (+ later: register_channel, ...)\nnative plugins call this inside register(api)" as PLUGINAPI #E2E2E2
  rectangle "DISCOVERY + INSTALL\ndrop-in dir: ~/.agentd/plugins/<id>/\n+ pip entry-points: group = 'agentd.plugins'\ninstall on demand -> catalog rebuilds (or `agentd plugin add`)" as DISCOVERY #FFE0B2
}

' ===========================================================================
' MCP MACHINERY - reused for BOTH internal and plugin MCP
' ===========================================================================
package "MCP MACHINERY  (reused)  ·  infrastructure/tools/mcp" #E8F8FF {
  rectangle "MCP provider  [now]\nlaunch / connect a server -> discover its tools\n-> wrap each as a Tool (see mcp-architecture.puml)" as MCP_PROV #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' MAIN - composition root: assemble the one catalog
' ===========================================================================
package "MAIN - composition root  ·  main/container.py" #FDECEA {
  rectangle "build_catalog(config, deps)   [generalize build_tools + _discover_mcp_tools]\n internal_native + internal_mcp + plugin_native + plugin_mcp\n -> wrap all in GuardedTool -> apply ENABLEMENT -> ONE [Tool] for the catalog" as BUILD #FBD9D4
}

' ===========================================================================
' ENABLEMENT - config-driven on/off, uniform across ALL sources, decoupled
' ===========================================================================
package "ENABLEMENT  (config · uniform · decoupled)  [net-new]" #FFF3E0 {
  rectangle "1) [plugins] <id> = on | off   (LOAD gate)\noff => plugin never discovered / imported -> its heavy deps never load" as TGL_PLUG #FFE0B2
  rectangle "2) [tools] enabled / disabled   (GLOBAL, by name/glob)\nturns ANY tool on/off platform-wide -- applied IDENTICALLY to all 4 sources\n(internal+plugin, native+mcp). A pure DATA filter on the catalog." as TGL_TOOLS #FFE0B2
  rectangle "3) agent.toml [tools] allow / deny   (PER-AGENT scope)  [now]\nwhich tools THIS agent sees (domain.select_tools)" as TGL_AGENT #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' EDGES
' ===========================================================================
AGENT --> CATALOG : select_tools(catalog, agent)\n(per-agent allow / deny)
CATALOG ..> P_TOOL : every entry implements
BUILD --> CATALOG : assembles + GuardedTool

' sources -> how each becomes a Tool
IN_NATIVE --> BUILD : Tool classes
IN_MCP --> MCP_PROV
PL_NATIVE --> PLUGINAPI : register_tool(...)
PL_MCP --> MCP_PROV
MCP_PROV --> BUILD : wrapped Tool(s)
PLUGINAPI --> BUILD : Tool(s)

' plugin system wiring
DISCOVERY --> BUILD : discovered plugins (active)
PL_NATIVE ..> MANIFEST : kind=native
PL_MCP ..> MANIFEST : kind=mcp
MANIFEST ..> DISCOVERY : declares entry / server

' enablement - three independent, config-driven layers (nothing coupled in code)
TGL_PLUG ..> DISCOVERY : load / skip (dep isolation)
TGL_TOOLS ..> BUILD : filter the catalog (uniform, by name)
TGL_AGENT ..> AGENT : per-agent allow / deny

note bottom of TGL_TOOLS
  DECOUPLED: enable/disable is DATA applied at the
  catalog filter -- adding/removing a tool is a
  CONFIG line, never a code change. No tool is wired
  to a feature `if`; all plug in/out independently.
  (Dependency availability -- e.g. browser needs an
  engine -- is orthogonal, not coupling.)
end note

note right of CATALOG
  "Behaves exactly like an internal tool":
  guaranteed by NORMALIZATION -- a plugin
  yields Tool objects that join the same list
  and pass through the same select_tools.
  The ONLY differences vs internal:
    * where the code lives (shipped vs downloaded)
    * when it loads (eager vs on-demand / lazy)
end note

note bottom of PL_MCP
  HEAVY DEPS STAY OUT OF CORE (both kinds):
   * native plugin -> deps in its OWN package,
     lazy `import` only when activated.
   * mcp plugin    -> deps in a SEPARATE PROCESS,
     never in agentd's venv.
  Core ships only the lightweight INTERNAL set.
  (Mirrors OpenClaw: a package per extension,
   bundleRuntimeDependencies:false, lazy import.)
end note

legend bottom
  | Color | Meaning |
  | green | exists in v2 today |
  | amber | net-new (plugin system) |
  | gray  | port = interface |
  | blue  | the catalog / Tool port |
  | 2x2   | rows = internal/plugin · cols = native/mcp |
endlegend

@enduml
